msgstr "Callers submit bounded slots; one owner services the controller and endpoints"

msgid "Queue capacity, callbacks and storage are explicit; stop admission, drain accepted slots and controller references, join observers, then destroy the owner"
msgstr "Queue capacity, callbacks and storage are explicit; stop admission, drain accepted slots and controller references, join observers, then destroy the owner"

msgid "These are application choices, not three hidden driver workers. Product examples live in [nexus-examples](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus-examples): `templates/{native,qiming,sky,liangshan}`, `apps/shared_spi_runtime` and `apps/stream_recovery`. Use their README with the fixed examples revision associated with your platform. The SPI Native example and FreeRTOS POSIX-host exercise are separate scopes; Native Platform does not accept `backend = \"freertos\"`. A software two-CS fixture does not establish a second physical CS on a launch board."
msgstr "These are application choices, not three hidden driver workers. Product examples live in [nexus-examples](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus-examples): `templates/{native,qiming,sky,liangshan}`, `apps/shared_spi_runtime` and `apps/stream_recovery`. Use their README with the fixed examples revision associated with your platform. The SPI Native example and FreeRTOS POSIX-host exercise are separate scopes; Native Platform does not accept `backend = \"freertos\"`. A software two-CS fixture does not establish a second physical CS on a launch board."

msgid "For finite requests, REJECTED retains no caller references. ACCEPTED borrows request and transfer storage until acquire-observed SETTLED. Cancel and deadline expiry request progress toward withdrawal; they do not settle the request. QUARANTINED preserves storage and cleanup obligations. SETTLED does not imply a successful transfer or that callbacks and observers have already joined. Read [ownership](../explanation/ownership.md) before placing asynchronous storage on a stack or stopping a worker."
msgstr "For finite requests, REJECTED retains no caller references. ACCEPTED borrows request and transfer storage until acquire-observed SETTLED. Cancel and deadline expiry request progress toward withdrawal; they do not settle the request. QUARANTINED preserves storage and cleanup obligations. SETTLED does not imply a successful transfer or that callbacks and observers have already joined. Read [ownership](../explanation/ownership.md) before placing asynchronous storage on a stack or stopping a worker."

msgid "For several authoritative predicates sharing one wait port, `nx_wait_select` checks a caller-owned source array from an explicit cyclic start index. It returns an observed-ready index without acquiring or consuming that source. The caller chooses fairness by advancing the next start index, wires every publisher to the same port, and owns service/timer progress. Stop and join publishers and waiters before reclaiming their state. There is no implicit subscription, dispatch, worker or resource transfer; the public {ref}`wait contract <wait_8h>` still governs arm/recheck and the absolute deadline."
msgstr "For several authoritative predicates sharing one wait port, `nx_wait_select` checks a caller-owned source array from an explicit cyclic start index. It returns an observed-ready index without acquiring or consuming that source. The caller chooses fairness by advancing the next start index, wires every publisher to the same port, and owns service/timer progress. Stop and join publishers and waiters before reclaiming their state. There is no implicit subscription, dispatch, worker or resource transfer; the public {ref}`wait contract <wait_8h>` still governs arm/recheck and the absolute deadline."

msgid "For streams, a consumer releases each acquired block explicitly. Slow consumers can cause loss or stop on backpressure according to the selected mode; providers must not overwrite outstanding loans. Stop may return BUSY until loans and hardware references drain. Restart uses a new valid lifecycle after complete stop; clearing counters is not recovery. The H743 continuous-mode exercise is a separate exact ARM configuration, not a claim that the three launch boards have identical continuous-mode wiring."
msgstr "For streams, a consumer releases each acquired block explicitly. Slow consumers can cause loss or stop on backpressure according to the selected mode; providers must not overwrite outstanding loans. Stop may return BUSY until loans and hardware references drain. Restart uses a new valid lifecycle after complete stop; clearing counters is not recovery. The H743 continuous-mode exercise is a separate exact ARM configuration, not a claim that the three launch boards have identical continuous-mode wiring."

msgid "Diagnose facts without changing ownership"
msgstr "Diagnose facts without changing ownership"

msgid "`nx_io_diagnose` in `nexus/io/diagnostic.h` composes copied request and stream observations with explicitly known lifecycle, owner, service-time and observer facts. It neither reads live MMIO nor invokes service or recovery. Its independent finding bits can coexist; `unknown_facts` preserves missing information. No findings does not certify health."
msgstr "`nx_io_diagnose` in `nexus/io/diagnostic.h` composes copied request and stream observations with explicitly known lifecycle, owner, service-time and observer facts. It neither reads live MMIO nor invokes service or recovery. Its independent finding bits can coexist; `unknown_facts` preserves missing information. No findings does not certify health."

msgid "A request that stops advancing does not prove the service loop was omitted. `SERVICE_OVERDUE` requires finite timestamps in the same monotonic domain and a positive declared maximum gap; reversed time rejects with STATE. Owner admission fields are known only after a successful owner diagnostic snapshot. BUSY alone does not prove a full queue. Outstanding stream blocks can be producer, ready or consumer loans; the ordinary cursor says nothing about a private preposted slot. Application escalation still owns retry, safe outputs and reset policy."
msgstr "A request that stops advancing does not prove the service loop was omitted. `SERVICE_OVERDUE` requires finite timestamps in the same monotonic domain and a positive declared maximum gap; reversed time rejects with STATE. Owner admission fields are known only after a successful owner diagnostic snapshot. BUSY alone does not prove a full queue. Outstanding stream blocks can be producer, ready or consumer loans; the ordinary cursor says nothing about a private preposted slot. Application escalation still owns retry, safe outputs and reset policy."

msgid "`nx_dma_storage_validate` checks the complete explicit reservation separately from its payload. For example, a 17-byte payload may use a caller-owned 64-byte reservation aligned to 32-byte cache lines. The entire reservation must already fit its declared DMA-visible domain and whole-line ownership. The helper does not round, allocate, bounce, perform cache maintenance or replace provider mode admission. Deadline expiry never permits reusing the reservation before drain."
msgstr "`nx_dma_storage_validate` checks the complete explicit reservation separately from its payload. For example, a 17-byte payload may use a caller-owned 64-byte reservation aligned to 32-byte cache lines. The entire reservation must already fit its declared DMA-visible domain and whole-line ownership. The helper does not round, allocate, bounce, perform cache maintenance or replace provider mode admission. Deadline expiry never permits reusing the reservation before drain."

msgid "The optional owner observation adds `accepting`, `queued` and `slot_available`. Recompile consumers because its public observation/sidecar layout changed. Default owner and provider structures do not gain these fields. Measure optional sidecar storage for the selected ABI; it is not assumed to be free."
msgstr "The optional owner observation adds `accepting`, `queued` and `slot_available`. Recompile consumers because its public observation/sidecar layout changed. Default owner and provider structures do not gain these fields. Measure optional sidecar storage for the selected ABI; it is not assumed to be free."

msgid "Plan daily device operations separately from qualification"
msgstr "Plan daily device operations separately from qualification"

msgid "For flash/debug, use an identified equipment file and provenance from the actual successful build. Monitor may run without build association:"
msgstr "For flash/debug, use an identified equipment file and provenance from the actual successful build. Monitor may run without build association:"

msgid "The default prints a plan. Actual execution requires `--execute --output` with a new owned directory. Flash/debug require matching board/part, image, probe serial and pinned tool/configuration bytes; they do not require a serial console. Monitor requires the board, stable serial by-id and station lock, but may omit build provenance: that result states `image_linkage = unassociated`, not an image-qualified observation. Monitor uses the explicitly selected host-supported standard baud rate with 8N1 and finite duration; 115200 remains the default. Unknown rates or a TTY configuration mismatch fail rather than selecting a different speed. Host acceptance does not prove the physical device baud rate. EOF or disconnection fails. Debug binds loopback. Failed or cancelled device operations retain their locks for explicit inspection; normal completion releases them. A successful daily operation does not qualify HIL. Until real equipment is connected, record physical execution as `not_executed`. The [performance and HIL guide](performance-hil.md) owns capture and qualification."
msgstr "The default prints a plan. Actual execution requires `--execute --output` with a new owned directory. Flash/debug require matching board/part, image, probe serial and pinned tool/configuration bytes; they do not require a serial console. Monitor requires the board, stable serial by-id and station lock, but may omit build provenance: that result states `image_linkage = unassociated`, not an image-qualified observation. Monitor uses the explicitly selected host-supported standard baud rate with 8N1 and finite duration; 115200 remains the default. Unknown rates or a TTY configuration mismatch fail rather than selecting a different speed. Host acceptance does not prove the physical device baud rate. EOF or disconnection fails. Debug binds loopback. Failed or cancelled device operations retain their locks for explicit inspection; normal completion releases them. A successful daily operation does not qualify HIL. Until real equipment is connected, record physical execution as `not_executed`. The [performance and HIL guide](performance-hil.md) owns capture and qualification."

msgid "For one bounded Linux batch, add `--client` to `debug`. This uses the official GDB/OpenOCD pipe transport and rejects `--port`; the default debug server keeps its loopback TCP workflow. The target JSON must explicitly identify the GDB executable in `gdb_client.tool` with `path`, `size` and `sha256`. Optional `gdb_client.commands` uses the same file identity fields and replaces the default `info threads` command. Review that file as executable operator input. GDB starts with automatic scripts disabled, loads the exact provenance-bound ELF, attaches, runs the selected commands and detaches. Tool/configuration/ELF identities are checked before and after execution. The finite timeout covers the owned process chain; failure or cancellation withdraws it and retains station quarantine. No executable or target is auto-discovered. See the [development tool contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/dev/README.md) for the equipment schema and command example. Host pipe fixtures do not establish physical probe support."
msgstr "For one bounded Linux batch, add `--client` to `debug`. This uses the official GDB/OpenOCD pipe transport and rejects `--port`; the default debug server keeps its loopback TCP workflow. The target JSON must explicitly identify the GDB executable in `gdb_client.tool` with `path`, `size` and `sha256`. Optional `gdb_client.commands` uses the same file identity fields and replaces the default `info threads` command. Review that file as executable operator input. GDB starts with automatic scripts disabled, loads the exact provenance-bound ELF, attaches, runs the selected commands and detaches. Tool/configuration/ELF identities are checked before and after execution. The finite timeout covers the owned process chain; failure or cancellation withdraws it and retains station quarantine. No executable or target is auto-discovered. See the [development tool contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/dev/README.md) for the equipment schema and command example. Host pipe fixtures do not establish physical probe support."

msgid "Development monitor remains Linux/POSIX. The session-bound terminal phases are `acquiring`, `owned`, `releasing` and `released`. After confirmed helper withdrawal, the parent may restore its originally held descriptor only when `owned` proves this session's exclusive ownership. An already `released` helper does not authorize another restore or exclusive-release operation: another process may now own the terminal. Unknown, corrupt or intermediate phases, unconfirmed withdrawal and identity failures retain quarantine without touching another owner's terminal. The parent never opens a replacement by-id device."
msgstr "Development monitor remains Linux/POSIX. The session-bound terminal phases are `acquiring`, `owned`, `releasing` and `released`. After confirmed helper withdrawal, the parent may restore its originally held descriptor only when `owned` proves this session's exclusive ownership. An already `released` helper does not authorize another restore or exclusive-release operation: another process may now own the terminal. Unknown, corrupt or intermediate phases, unconfirmed withdrawal and identity failures retain quarantine without touching another owner's terminal. The parent never opens a replacement by-id device."

msgid "Primary I/O failure and cleanup failure remain separately visible, including their exception cause/context chains; a cleanup exception must not hide an earlier EOF or read failure. Independent cleanup errors remain in the operation record. External SIGKILL of the parent cannot guarantee restoration. The baud-rate extension does not expand formal HIL console admission or establish Windows/macOS support. See the [serial ownership regressions](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/testing/test_dev_serial_ownership.py) and [rate/cancellation regressions](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/testing/test_dev_serial_rates.py)."
msgstr "Primary I/O failure and cleanup failure remain separately visible, including their exception cause/context chains; a cleanup exception must not hide an earlier EOF or read failure. Independent cleanup errors remain in the operation record. External SIGKILL of the parent cannot guarantee restoration. The baud-rate extension does not expand formal HIL console admission or establish Windows/macOS support. See the [serial ownership regressions](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/testing/test_dev_serial_ownership.py) and [rate/cancellation regressions](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/tools/testing/test_dev_serial_rates.py)."
